 # DM-NeRF
-
-
 ## Overview
-DM-NeRF is a pipeline that simultaneously reconstructs continuous 3D scene geometry, decomposes all individual objects in 3D space, and supports flexible object shape manipulation (translation, rotation, size adjustment, deformation) from 2D images only [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard NeRF by introducing an explicit **object field** that predicts a one-hot object code for every 3D point, enabling instance-level editing without explicit mesh extraction [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Object Decomposition and Composition](14518-object-decomposition-and-composition.md) by using a learnable object code conditioned on spatial position rather than fixed segmentation masks.
-
+DM-NeRF is a pipeline that simultaneously reconstructs continuous 3D scene geometry, decomposes all individual objects in 3D space, and supports flexible object shape manipulation (translation, rotation, size adjustment, deformation) from 2D images only [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard NeRF by introducing an explicit object field that predicts a one-hot object code for every 3D point, enabling instance-level editing without explicit mesh extraction [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Object Decomposition and Composition](14518-object-decomposition-and-composition.md) by using a learnable object code conditioned on spatial position rather than fixed segmentation masks [S1, unofficial].
